cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Utility-Aware Occupancy Camouflage for Point Cloud Privacy: Pilot Release"
abstract: >-
  Code and per-frame numerical results for a scoped pilot on utility-aware occupancy
  camouflage: a deterministic, gradient-free sender-side defense that removes the
  lowest-utility fraction of occupied voxels in order to degrade an
  occupancy-based point-cloud reconstruction path. Released artifacts cover a fixed
  16-frame KITTI Velodyne subset across nine removal budgets.
type: software
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasmine8/utility-aware-occupancy-camouflage"
# `doi` is the Zenodo *concept* DOI: it always resolves to the newest archived
# version, so it stays correct no matter which release a reader lands on.
# Version-specific DOIs: v1.0.1 = 10.5281/zenodo.23320736; v1.0.2 is minted on
# publication of the release and is linked from the concept DOI record.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23320735"
keywords:
  - point clouds
  - model inversion
  - privacy
  - autonomous driving
  - KITTI
  - voxel features

authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Mingzhen"
    affiliation: "School of Software, Henan University of Engineering, Zhengzhou 451191, China"
